<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 10.198 percent from 10.216 percent at the previous auction on November 12.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: May 20, 1997 (May 13, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.198 percent (10.216)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 874.875 million (992.525 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 946.225 million (1.28 billion)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 10.101-10.240 percent (9.999-10.247)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 10.101-10.400 percent (9.999-10.600)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 123 (174)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 137 (215)</p>
<p>($1 = 3.40 Egyptian pounds)</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
